[{:db/id "q-8845/selection/cf928b244b906a536fe1971670c307724be8e4757ef003a1695a5be4fdfff8cd" :answer/id #uuid "871ce93b-ec12-5286-8bd4-67627201c2d0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=K(2+{e}^{3x})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8845/selection/6e7ffee41e05872af16384961ff8ba35e9929f65b18851fc9f286d4302fcd988" :answer/id #uuid "57471787-4f08-5881-8b35-06861226bcce" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y={x}^{2}+{e}^{Kx}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8845/selection/66cc1785204d3e51518c32006d05b0f5b35b9ba687493fdf05ca5e37b18235f2" :answer/id #uuid "3dc3795f-ec02-5824-98cc-23dcf3965117" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=K{x}^{2}+{e}^{x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8845/selection/c24649ad2ba8cfba0344828b6a1daecf137de5bb373674071f129a2e67aada30" :answer/id #uuid "ceefc40f-a105-555d-9a11-ac489d4cb5d1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=K{e}^{x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8845/selection/1f4c61a1879c6fa472221fe516efe2e7cd6db6576e9e9e058837758143b642c3" :answer/id #uuid "72bfbf59-db54-5c23-9b71-10aa88eece49" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=x{e}^{Kx}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8845/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "f578f94a-1131-5692-995d-02a333ecc2f1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-8845/selection/1f4c61a1879c6fa472221fe516efe2e7cd6db6576e9e9e058837758143b642c3" :answer-field/choices ["q-8845/selection/cf928b244b906a536fe1971670c307724be8e4757ef003a1695a5be4fdfff8cd" "q-8845/selection/6e7ffee41e05872af16384961ff8ba35e9929f65b18851fc9f286d4302fcd988" "q-8845/selection/66cc1785204d3e51518c32006d05b0f5b35b9ba687493fdf05ca5e37b18235f2" "q-8845/selection/c24649ad2ba8cfba0344828b6a1daecf137de5bb373674071f129a2e67aada30" "q-8845/selection/1f4c61a1879c6fa472221fe516efe2e7cd6db6576e9e9e058837758143b642c3"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-8845" :question/id #uuid "1a788c8d-223d-5e9b-9a2b-46f1e25dd2ff" :question/math-academy-id "q-8845" :question/problem "Use the transformation $y=v(x)x$ to find the general solution of the following homogeneous differential equation.\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{y}{x}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{y}{x})+1)\n$$" :question/worked-solution "With $y=v(x)x$, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x) \\\\  & =x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our differential equation gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{y}{x}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{y}{x})+1) \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v & =\\frac{vx}{x}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{vx}{x})+1) \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v & =v(\\operatorname{ln}⁡v+1) \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v & =v\\operatorname{ln}⁡v+v \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} & =v\\operatorname{ln}⁡v \\\\ \\frac{1}{v\\operatorname{ln}⁡v}\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrating both sides with respect to $x$, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{v\\operatorname{ln}⁡v}\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{v\\operatorname{ln}⁡v}\\,\\text{d}v & =\\int \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTo evaluate the integral on the left-hand side, we use integration by substitution with\n\n$$\nu=\\operatorname{ln}⁡v,\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}v}=\\frac{1}{v}.\n$$\n\nWe now proceed to solve the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{v\\operatorname{ln}⁡v}\\,\\text{d}v & =\\int \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{u}\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}v}\\,\\text{d}v & =\\int \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡|u| & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+C \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{ln}⁡v| & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the transformation $y=vx$, we get\n\n$$\nv=\\frac{y}{x}\\,.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our solution, we finally obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{ln}⁡v| & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+C \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\frac{y}{x}| & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+C \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\frac{y}{x}| & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+\\operatorname{ln}⁡{e}^{C} \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\frac{y}{x}| & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{C}|x|) \\\\ |\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\frac{y}{x}| & =|x|{e}^{C} \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡\\frac{y}{x} & =\\pm {e}^{C}x \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡\\frac{y}{x} & =Kx \\\\ \\frac{y}{x} & ={e}^{Kx} \\\\ y & =x{e}^{Kx}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that we introduced the new constant of integration:\n\n$$\nK=\\pm {e}^{C}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-8845/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "49eaf082-07de-5468-a2d7-4cdfce27a553"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-8845"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-14318/selection/ed03caa38430e5ddbae5bac17d759b99ab7891589f9c215072bbb1bc6c291c40" :answer/id #uuid "d704103b-8247-507d-a7b9-61e183bffa8e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|-\\frac{y}{x}=C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-14318/selection/4f6a3aedfa359eb8f4d9a45ec6f07fca326fb008bbebceeecc702595538fd162" :answer/id #uuid "acd76bfd-2b48-5555-951d-718d17e96d89" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\frac{y}{{x}^{2}}|+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{x}^{2}}=C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-14318/selection/74ba16975b64ac1345af2255f3002982d88a37ecc2b6b3c00e2a2b12c812fa3f" :answer/id #uuid "a43acb57-ccce-5d10-915d-4ab752711bb4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{y}^{2}}=C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-14318/selection/a79dd5ffb93084ca57a6888cbddcbbe2c7dbedcb1cd39893d091e6707c4341a0" :answer/id #uuid "a8d3d60c-6b7c-536d-8232-0c3fa067f472" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{x}^{3}}|-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{y}^{2}}=C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-14318/selection/83bf18a9404c1de26d6978b11e7bdc68a5666c9c5789ced481ef05c2e231242b" :answer/id #uuid "8a6912e4-ff1e-5b9f-b547-4b40e3187c2e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\frac{{x}^{3}}{y}|+2\\frac{y}{x}=C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-14318/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "b7cccb1f-65f3-5787-9990-3a1c7d1f77e6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-14318/selection/74ba16975b64ac1345af2255f3002982d88a37ecc2b6b3c00e2a2b12c812fa3f" :answer-field/choices ["q-14318/selection/ed03caa38430e5ddbae5bac17d759b99ab7891589f9c215072bbb1bc6c291c40" "q-14318/selection/4f6a3aedfa359eb8f4d9a45ec6f07fca326fb008bbebceeecc702595538fd162" "q-14318/selection/74ba16975b64ac1345af2255f3002982d88a37ecc2b6b3c00e2a2b12c812fa3f" "q-14318/selection/a79dd5ffb93084ca57a6888cbddcbbe2c7dbedcb1cd39893d091e6707c4341a0" "q-14318/selection/83bf18a9404c1de26d6978b11e7bdc68a5666c9c5789ced481ef05c2e231242b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-14318" :question/id #uuid "229ab31e-f5e5-5234-93bf-ecaf044e3397" :question/math-academy-id "q-14318" :question/problem "Use the transformation $y=v(x)x$ to find the general solution of the following homogeneous differential equation.\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{yx}{{y}^{2}+{x}^{2}}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "With $y=v(x)x$, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x) \\\\  & =x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our differential equation gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{yx}{{y}^{2}+{x}^{2}} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v & =\\frac{(vx)x}{(vx)^{2}+{x}^{2}} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v & =\\frac{v{x}^{2}}{{x}^{2}({v}^{2}+1)} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{v}{{v}^{2}+1}-v \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{v-{v}^{3}-v}{{v}^{2}+1} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{-{v}^{3}}{{v}^{2}+1} \\\\ \\frac{{v}^{2}+1}{{v}^{3}}\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{1}{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrating both sides with respect to $x$, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{v}^{2}+1}{{v}^{3}}\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =-\\int \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int (\\frac{1}{v}+\\frac{1}{{v}^{3}})\\,\\text{d}v & =-\\int \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡|v|-\\frac{1}{2{v}^{2}} & =-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+{C}_{1} \\\\ 2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|v|-\\frac{1}{{v}^{2}} & =-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+2{C}_{1} \\\\ 2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|v|-\\frac{1}{{v}^{2}} & =-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that we introduced $C=2{C}_{1}.$\n\nFrom the transformation $y=vx$, we get\n\n$$\nv=\\frac{y}{x}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our solution, we finally obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\frac{y}{x}|-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{y}^{2}} & =-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+C \\\\ 2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\frac{y}{x}|+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{y}^{2}} & =C \\\\ 2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{y}^{2}} & =C\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-14318/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "49eaf082-07de-5468-a2d7-4cdfce27a553"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-14318"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-14322/selection/9303c8fb4e081f18d8684f2fe842d6e75dd3a0f5657a50bcaef6d8c54a688d33" :answer/id #uuid "886d1cb9-651e-55c3-8dd7-f0cd516ec217" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{4{x}^{2}y}{{x}^{3}+x{y}^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-14322/selection/f1690f9d5e7a0ee3b372b31011c533bd9a01b029f1344b34e89782eb64cc8bbc" :answer/id #uuid "44afc39f-e195-5a49-b77f-1a6b7858a92e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x+y}{y})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-14322/selection/638e0eb5346792c48c64dd8c8fc1fd46727cf81d96815e639d3353716f6fe72a" :answer/id #uuid "5c94aa24-b4aa-5294-8d6b-45a136c59aa5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{{x}^{2}+1}{{y}^{2}+xy}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-14322/selection/20d98c86088b8a73886be5300b0f32d44a1ca486dc8085ee900cb88f196a7292" :answer/id #uuid "6865b4dc-bb1b-58ce-a871-56fabaa9d0b8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={e}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{y})}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-14322/selection/779ab5b1bda699eaf4f26cc844b1040c549ccca09671547c333a0b4b53215be0" :answer/id #uuid "9be4c937-7a50-5044-be2d-dc56e02f18b9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{xy}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-14322/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "7ff28647-7053-5c93-a365-e7beed2ca160" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-14322/selection/638e0eb5346792c48c64dd8c8fc1fd46727cf81d96815e639d3353716f6fe72a" :answer-field/choices ["q-14322/selection/9303c8fb4e081f18d8684f2fe842d6e75dd3a0f5657a50bcaef6d8c54a688d33" "q-14322/selection/f1690f9d5e7a0ee3b372b31011c533bd9a01b029f1344b34e89782eb64cc8bbc" "q-14322/selection/638e0eb5346792c48c64dd8c8fc1fd46727cf81d96815e639d3353716f6fe72a" "q-14322/selection/20d98c86088b8a73886be5300b0f32d44a1ca486dc8085ee900cb88f196a7292" "q-14322/selection/779ab5b1bda699eaf4f26cc844b1040c549ccca09671547c333a0b4b53215be0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-14322" :question/id #uuid "07cbf2f2-d5ef-5e3f-8e63-cd4b2886b3f6" :question/math-academy-id "q-14322" :question/problem "Which of the following is NOT a first-order homogeneous ordinary differential equation?" :question/worked-solution "A first-order ordinary differential equation that is written in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=f(x,y)\n$$\n\nis said to be homogeneous if it satisfies the following property:\n\n$$\nf(tx,ty)=f(x,y)\\,\n$$\n\nThe only option in which this is NOT the case is:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{{x}^{2}+1}{{y}^{2}+xy}\n$$\n\nWe can check this using one of two methods.\n\n**Method 1**\n\nLet $f(x,y)=\\frac{{x}^{2}+1}{{y}^{2}+xy}.$\n\nWe see that the numerator is NOT a homogeneous polynomial. Therefore, $f(x,y)$ is NOT a homogeneous function.\n\nHence, the original differential equation is  NOT homogeneous.\n\n**Method 2**\n\nTo check this in detail using the definition, we first write:\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\frac{{x}^{2}+1}{{y}^{2}+xy}\\,\n$$\n\nWe can check that this is not homogeneous showing that $f(tx,ty)\\ne f(x,y),$ as follows:\n\nFor $x=1$, $y=2$ and $t=3$, for instance, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(tx,ty) & =f(2\\cdot 1,2\\cdot 3) \\\\  & =f(2,6) \\\\  & =\\frac{{2}^{2}+1}{{6}^{2}+2(6)} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{48}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y) & =f(1,2) \\\\  & =\\frac{{1}^{2}+1}{{2}^{2}+1(2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn other words, there exists at least one combination of values of $x$, $y$ and $t$ for which the identity $f(tx,ty)=f(x,y)$ is not observed.\n\nHence, the original differential equation is  NOT homogeneous." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-14322/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e8c2a855-07a3-5855-9f6c-1a914953ac53"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-14322"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-14323/selection/232507774999ab46e2ab9e34c8804b4b5d64eee490f9de175151fbe1c83df031" :answer/id #uuid "877429e0-f6c3-5e38-ac9e-9a63efc0ed8b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{v+2}{1-3v-2{v}^{2}}\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-14323/selection/7cd8671da2d0e5a5944f30a6a9d024b46f7b85029b73d6a593a31281cf5668a2" :answer/id #uuid "19c39017-c049-534c-be7c-e97383d4c2dd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1-2v-3{v}^{2}}{{v}^{2}+2v}\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-14323/selection/9d25c3617cc27e0368b47b035c357947c369563ee6abd63e518e81311fe9062f" :answer/id #uuid "cfb88851-5f78-508f-b23e-65272f51e213" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{v}^{2}-1}{1-2{v}^{3}}\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-14323/selection/04f3567a10a7ee9703d8e211fab2a5fb0f650ced067f15954fa87786bb3c05b4" :answer/id #uuid "49a1ff16-6933-5a69-a8ae-d7cff266954f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{v}^{3}+2{v}^{2}}{1-{v}^{2}}\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-14323/selection/792651016b158029335748718082947a3868f045760004e2a16e9b8a375a3d9a" :answer/id #uuid "8c75faa8-297d-53b1-a93d-56bbf35438ee" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{v}^{2}+2v}{1-{v}^{2}-2{v}^{3}}\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-14323/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "2a51ca83-20ab-506e-8203-e11a1404252a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-14323/selection/792651016b158029335748718082947a3868f045760004e2a16e9b8a375a3d9a" :answer-field/choices ["q-14323/selection/232507774999ab46e2ab9e34c8804b4b5d64eee490f9de175151fbe1c83df031" "q-14323/selection/7cd8671da2d0e5a5944f30a6a9d024b46f7b85029b73d6a593a31281cf5668a2" "q-14323/selection/9d25c3617cc27e0368b47b035c357947c369563ee6abd63e518e81311fe9062f" "q-14323/selection/04f3567a10a7ee9703d8e211fab2a5fb0f650ced067f15954fa87786bb3c05b4" "q-14323/selection/792651016b158029335748718082947a3868f045760004e2a16e9b8a375a3d9a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-14323" :question/id #uuid "ac3cbdaf-bfc0-50ab-89f3-54af7a9e11ba" :question/math-academy-id "q-14323" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{{x}^{3}+x{y}^{2}-{y}^{3}}{x{y}^{2}+2y{x}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nIf the transformation $y=v(x)x$ is applied to the differential equation, what is the resulting equation?" :question/worked-solution "Using the transformation $y=vx$ (where $v=v(x)$), we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x) \\\\  & =x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the given differential equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{{x}^{3}+x{y}^{2}-{y}^{3}}{x{y}^{2}+2y{x}^{2}} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v & =\\frac{{x}^{3}+x(vx)^{2}-(vx)^{3}}{x(vx)^{2}+2(vx){x}^{2}} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v & =\\frac{{x}^{3}(1+{v}^{2}-{v}^{3})}{{x}^{3}({v}^{2}+2v)} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v & =\\frac{1+{v}^{2}-{v}^{3}}{{v}^{2}+2v} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1+{v}^{2}-{v}^{3}}{{v}^{2}+2v}-v \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1+{v}^{2}-{v}^{3}-{v}^{3}-2{v}^{2}}{{v}^{2}+2v} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1-{v}^{2}-2{v}^{3}}{{v}^{2}+2v} \\\\ \\frac{{v}^{2}+2v}{1-{v}^{2}-2{v}^{3}}\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-14323/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a8edbecf-59d3-5f32-a0ac-d6e8f2128dc0"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-14323"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-90601/selection/754f75ee692e775313842c5c3e3891460f7e9d038c451060f92f866c813953a9" :answer/id #uuid "0ff11460-f786-59a3-b4f9-a60f3f9b9087" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡v}\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=-\\frac{2}{x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-90601/selection/460c022d8da952a7eb149b42a5ca008c9b85313d74279559670a2e2b49080c28" :answer/id #uuid "b3ed4c10-f1c2-5dba-85c3-82e0983dc72f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(2v-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{1}{v}))\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-90601/selection/1a68d4db340d12b80124b2759d19c32b18e94d2880dda6e2e146adc668defafe" :answer/id #uuid "918648d5-0bc1-51c8-a14c-0091e6104fbf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{v-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡v}\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-90601/selection/aff6030eacb168bb678a5a093246c1a97ce722aad576d554f7fe534624808e10" :answer/id #uuid "ef440ff9-b09e-5510-a6e6-6ecefbb2c7aa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{1}{v})\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=-\\frac{2}{x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-90601/selection/343cd0294684f07d9b12409a1eb1e353080dc76c360479049b84370d121a9896" :answer/id #uuid "167ceb5c-3fc1-58a1-ad1b-f9d3c81a9daf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡v}\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-90601/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "3dafc709-78bd-59b0-8297-e6c0a1b0d5b6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-90601/selection/754f75ee692e775313842c5c3e3891460f7e9d038c451060f92f866c813953a9" :answer-field/choices ["q-90601/selection/754f75ee692e775313842c5c3e3891460f7e9d038c451060f92f866c813953a9" "q-90601/selection/460c022d8da952a7eb149b42a5ca008c9b85313d74279559670a2e2b49080c28" "q-90601/selection/1a68d4db340d12b80124b2759d19c32b18e94d2880dda6e2e146adc668defafe" "q-90601/selection/aff6030eacb168bb678a5a093246c1a97ce722aad576d554f7fe534624808e10" "q-90601/selection/343cd0294684f07d9b12409a1eb1e353080dc76c360479049b84370d121a9896"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-90601" :question/id #uuid "0219c95b-5fe2-5772-a6bc-8e6a261c2490" :question/math-academy-id "q-90601" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{y}{x}-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{y}{x}).\n$$\n\nIf the transformation $y=v(x)x$ is applied to the differential equation, what is the resulting equation?" :question/worked-solution "Using the transformation $y=vx$ (where $v=v(x)$), we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x) \\\\  & =x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the given differential equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{y}{x}-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{y}{x}) \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v & =\\frac{vx}{x}-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{vx}{x}) \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v & =v-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡v \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} & =-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡v \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡v}\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{2}{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-90601/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a8edbecf-59d3-5f32-a0ac-d6e8f2128dc0"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-90601"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
